    <!--  Formatting broken when using enter so it has to be a one liner  -->
    <string name="privacy_page">Privacy Policy\nEffective Date: October 3, 2025\n\nShuttle Tracker (“the App”) respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle your information.\n\nInformation We Collect\nThe App may access your device location in order to:\n\nShow you the closest shuttle stop.\nCalculate how far you are from that stop.\n\nWe do not collect, store, or transmit your location data or any other personal information. All processing happens locally on your device.\n\nUse of Information\nLocation data is used only in real time to display shuttle stop information.\n\nYour location data is never stored, logged, or sent to our servers.\n\nSharing of Information\nWe do not share your location or any other personal information with third parties.\n\nChildren’s Privacy\nShuttle Tracker does not knowingly collect, store, or share personal information from children.\n\nChanges to This Policy\nIf we make changes to this Privacy Policy, we will update it here and revise the “Effective Date” above.\n\nContact Us\nIf you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, you can contact us at:\nJoel McCandless\nmail@joelmccandless.com</string>

    <string name="about_page">Shuttle Tracker is developed by the Rensselaer Center for Open Source
        by your fellow RPI students. As an open source application, anyone can help develop the RPI Shuttle Tracker
        regardless of experience! Any contributions are welcome, as well as feedback for our current team.
        If you would like to view our source code, click the button below and open our GitHub page, and you can
        open an \"issue\" to leave feedback for us. View our privacy policy with the button below.</string>

